# HeliosLM line-ending policy (v5.79).
#
# Several verification oracles pin sha256 digests of committed artifacts
# (benchmarks/calibration_board_2026-10-15.json "inputs",
# benchmarks/cost_per_completed_task_2026-10-13.json,
# benchmarks/std_bench_reference_2026-10-15.json subset hashes, and the
# byte-for-byte board rebuild in tests/test_calibration_board.py). Those
# digests are computed over LF content. On Windows checkouts with
# core.autocrlf=true the working tree becomes CRLF and every pinned
# digest "drifts" — the files differ only by line endings, so this is a
# checkout artifact, not data corruption.
#
# Fix: keep text files LF in the working tree on every platform
# (eol=lf), and mark known binary formats so they are never converted.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.zip  binary
*.gz   binary
*.pyc  binary
*.pt   binary
*.pth  binary
*.bin  binary
*.gguf binary
*.wav  binary
*.mp3  binary
*.mp4  binary
*.pdf  binary
